.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii timer_delete.2
.\"
.TH TIMER_DELETE 2 "July 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
timer_delete \- delete a POSIX per-process interval timer
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <time.h>
.PP
.BI "int timer_delete(timer_t " timerid ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR timer_delete ()
disarms and deletes the timer
.IR timerid ,
which must have been returned by a previous call to
.BR timer_create (2).
The timer id becomes invalid and its slot is freed for reuse.  Any pending
expiration notification that has not yet been accepted is discarded.
.PP
All of a process's timers are deleted automatically at
.BR execve (2)
and at process termination.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.  On error, \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I timerid
is not a valid, live timer.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timer_create (2),
.BR timer_settime (2),
.BR timer_gettime (2),
.BR timer_getoverrun (2)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2008.
